  "dn30:0.1": "",
  "dn30:0.2": "",
  "dn30:1.1.1": "The marks of the “five great men” are discussed in the later astrological text, Bṛhatsaṁhitā 69. ",
  "dn30:1.1.2": "",
  "dn30:1.1.3": "",
  "dn30:1.1.4": "",
  "dn30:1.1.5": "",
  "dn30:1.1.6": "",
  "dn30:1.1.7": "This is one of the latest suttas in the Pali Nikāyas. Typically this topic only comes up in relation to the Buddha’s fulfillment of Brahmanical prophecies. Here it is developed with a series of ornate verses, none of which have parallels. Nonetheless, it is worth noting that nowhere in the extensive discussions of the Buddha’s past good deeds is there any mention of the later concepts of the <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pāramīs</i> (“perfections”) or the Bodhisatta path. ",
  "dn30:1.1.8": "",
  "dn30:1.1.9": "",
  "dn30:1.1.10": "",
  "dn30:1.1.11": "",
  "dn30:1.1.12": "",
  "dn30:1.1.13": "",
  "dn30:1.2.1": "The marks are elsewhere listed in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn14/en/sujato#1.32.7'>DN 14:1.32.7</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn91/en/sujato#9.1'>MN 91:9.1</a>. I discuss the translation of the marks in my comments to DN 14. ",
