  "dn30:1.12.8": "",
  "dn30:1.12.9": "Whereas in the phrase <i lang='pi' translate='no'>brahmujugatto</i>, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>brahm-</i> means “extended, tall”, here <i lang='pi' translate='no'>brahmāva</i> means “like Brahmā”, either as a play on words or by mistaken etymology. ",
  "dn30:1.12.10": "",
  "dn30:1.12.11": "",
  "dn30:1.12.12": "",
  "dn30:1.12.13": "",
  "dn30:1.12.14": "This verse spoken by the soothsayers. ",
  "dn30:1.12.15": "",
  "dn30:1.12.16": "",
  "dn30:1.12.17": "",
  "dn30:1.13.0": "",
  "dn30:1.13.1": "",
  "dn30:1.13.2": "He receives bodily fullness as a result of giving food. ",
  "dn30:1.13.3": "",
  "dn30:1.13.4": "",
  "dn30:1.13.5": "",
  "dn30:1.14.1": "",
