  "dn30:1.16.3": "",
  "dn30:1.16.4": "",
  "dn30:1.16.5": "",
  "dn30:1.16.6": "“Tender” because he treated people tenderly; “serried” because his fingers and toes are kept gracefully together, not splayed and separated. ",
  "dn30:1.17.1": "",
  "dn30:1.17.2": "",
  "dn30:1.17.3": "“Inclusive and well-managed” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>saṅgahita</i>. It means “included”, as in those people who, due to the kindly actions, feel that they belong. For the sense “well-managed” see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an8.49/en/sujato#2.3'>AN 8.49:2.3</a>. Because of acting kindly and inclusively, people are well-disposed and work well together. ",
  "dn30:1.17.4": "",
  "dn30:1.17.5": "",
  "dn30:1.17.6": "",
  "dn30:1.17.7": "",
  "dn30:1.17.8": "",
  "dn30:1.18.1": "",
