  "dn30:1.29.7": "",
  "dn30:1.29.8": "",
  "dn30:1.30.1": "",
  "dn30:1.30.2": "For this positive sense of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>adhiṭṭhahi</i> compare <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an6.52/en/sujato#8.2'>AN 6.52:8.2</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn140/en/sujato#11.1'>MN 140:11.1</a>. ",
  "dn30:1.30.3": "",
  "dn30:1.30.4": "",
  "dn30:1.30.5": "There’s a play on <i lang='pi' translate='no'>abhivissaji</i> (“gave away”) and <i lang='pi' translate='no'>abhivassa</i> (“pouring rain”). ",
  "dn30:1.30.6": "",
  "dn30:1.30.7": "",
  "dn30:1.30.8": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kanaka</i>, one of the many Indic words for gold, is from the same Proto-Indo European root as the English word “honey”. ",
  "dn30:1.30.9": "",
  "dn30:1.30.10": "",
  "dn30:1.30.11": "",
  "dn30:1.30.12": "",
  "dn30:1.30.13": "",
  "dn30:1.30.14": "Here <i lang='pi' translate='no'>mokkha</i> = <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pāmokkha</i> (“chief, best”). ",
  "dn30:1.30.15": "",
  "dn30:1.30.16": "",
  "dn30:1.30.17": "",
